 ## Configuration and safeguards
 
-Conductor uses `REMEDY_API_BASE_URL` and the existing gateway authentication configuration. Deploy the gateway recovery routes and bridge endpoints together with the Conductor changes. Preserve each deployment's environment files, compose overrides, networks, and persistent snapshot volume.
+Conductor uses `REMEDY_API_BASE_URL` and `REMEDY_API_KEY` (legacy aliases: `PROJECT_REMEDY_BASE_URL` and `PROJECT_REMEDY_API_KEY`). Deploy the gateway recovery routes and bridge endpoints together with the Conductor changes. Preserve each deployment's environment files, compose overrides, networks, and persistent snapshot volume.
 
 Bridge inference settings are documented in its `.env.example`. The shared client supports Ollama primary and OpenAI fallback for text, vision, and advanced agent tool calls. OpenAI tool calls use Responses, with tool-result and reasoning-context replay. Availability failures can trigger fallback; invalid requests and refusals do not.
 
@@ -46,3 +46,9 @@ Browser acceptance on 2026-09-13 covered task creation, source-image inference,
 ## Deployment notes
 
 The isolated `client/src/remediation-queue-entry.tsx` supports layering the same UI onto an existing compiled application. Normal source builds mount the component through `ProjectAccessibility.jsx`. The integration source is the durable handoff; environment-specific image tags and deployment credentials are managed separately.
+
+## Release references
+
+Matching component commits are Remedy Bridge `5d015f6981bc8ce125633c98af78e90ffffb9286` and Remedy Gateway `5893489cd84cdd38f1af59e7fed87c3a51d729d2`, published on `main` in their respective `johnnylibretexts` repositories. Use a fresh clone of the gateway repository when integrating this release; older checkouts have a different commit lineage.
+
+At publication on 2026-09-13, GitHub reported 33 dependency alerts for Remedy Bridge (3 critical, 11 high, 17 moderate, 2 low). These alerts were not triaged in the remediation acceptance run. Review the repository's dependency-security report before production promotion.
